{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/849744-where-actually-middle-world-and-upper-world-is","id":849744,"title":"Where actually Middle World and Upper World is?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-19T08:49:22-07:00","id":849744,"title":"Where actually Middle World and Upper World is?","content":"Hello, currently I have started to work on Nunnhei and Hsien. They both use the term Middle World or Kingdom. Where actually it is? Is it Middle umbra or Earth?. This is important because they Nunnhei can step sideways to Upper World. Then where upper world actually is? Is it Penumbra of Middle Umbra?. Hsien says they are creators of Middle Kingdom. Is it earth or middle umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T10:45:47-07:00","id":849790,"title":"","content":"The Hsien's Middle Kingdom is Asia (occasionally it's used to refer to Earth), with the Yang World as Asia's Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> For the Nunnehi, the Middle World is Earth, and the Upper World is the Middle Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T13:32:07-07:00","id":849852,"title":"","content":"&quot;Middle Kingdom&quot; is frequently used in Hengeyokai to refer to the entire physical being of the universe as well (In a sense of being between &quot;heaven&quot; and the land of the dead).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:19:55-07:00","id":849896,"title":"","content":"Then I can assume that nunnhei has nothing to do with high umbra. That relaxed me since I really don't want to read all that book of worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T22:01:12-07:00","id":850030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/849744-where-actually-middle-world-and-upper-world-is?p=849896#post849896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I can assume that nunnhei has nothing to do with high umbra. That relaxed me since I really don't want to read all that book of worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. I believe that the nunnehi setup rubbed more shoulders with Werewolf than Mage, so any old references you might see to the Deep Umbra in Changeling might be referring to what Mage calls (and W20 changed Werewolf to call) the High Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T01:15:44-07:00","id":850054,"title":"","content":"What about hsien? There are elements I guess, since I started to read just now, are there any relations? By the way changeling refers golden paths of balor which goes to high umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T18:01:48-07:00","id":851482,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, what do the beings of the Middle Kingdom call the High Umbra if the Low Umbra is the Yin World and the Middle Umbra is the Yang World? It feels quite ordered, in a Yin sort of way, but it's also got elements of Yang in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:28:13-07:00","id":851766,"title":"","content":"Well, actually in Book Of Worlds there is a section that tells us about &quot;Penumbra - Videre&quot;, and Hermetics says there is three perspective of it. Astral Videre, Videre Spiritus and Videre Mortem. Astral Videre. I am intepreting this as there is only one penumbra and three perspective of it. Also, book says you will see your appropriate perspective once you are there. I think kithian is categorizing worlds as penumbra expect for Earth. I mean if Middle Kingdom or Middle World is Earth, and Lower World/Kingdom is the Videre Mortem(Penumbra of Low Umbra), I think Upper World/Kingdom is changes.<br /> <br /> It is about perspective. I don't think any of Nunnhei can see the Astral Videre since they are primordial and Videre Spiritus is suits for them. However, in Hsien case it could be different. They could categorize both Videre Spiritus(Penumbra of Middle Umbra) and Astral Videre as one, and name it as Upper World.<br /> <br /> However, one other think is that &quot;High Umbra&quot; could be &quot;banal&quot;, since it is about concepts rather than individual dreams. Sometimes I think it as Dreaming's young evil twin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T22:08:25-07:00","id":852243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/849744-where-actually-middle-world-and-upper-world-is?p=851482#post851482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, what do the beings of the Middle Kingdom call the High Umbra if the Low Umbra is the Yin World and the Middle Umbra is the Yang World? It feels quite ordered, in a Yin sort of way, but it's also got elements of Yang in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>KotE and company ignored it, so as of yet, they don't call it anything. Also, Yin isn't really a force of order as such; stillness has some connection to order, but Yin is also coalescence and things of matter, so the High Umbra probably has very little of it. All in all, while the Middle Penumbra is called the Yang World and the Low Umbra is called the Yin World, it'd be weird for, say, Middle Umbra beings to have no Yin, since Yin is associated with Water and Metal elementals. Likewise, ghosts likely have some Passions that impart Yang to them. The simplified stat blocks in a lot of the books aren't a good way to apply Daoist theory to the WoD. But then, that's par for course, given the existence of Dragons of the East and its attempt to shoehorn the Triat (which really didn't even belong in that book, since it was about Mage) into Daoism. The end result was not pretty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, actually in Book Of Worlds there is a section that tells us about &quot;Penumbra - Videre&quot;, and Hermetics says there is three perspective of it. Astral Videre, Videre Spiritus and Videre Mortem. Astral Videre. I am intepreting this as there is only one penumbra and three perspective of it. Also, book says you will see your appropriate perspective once you are there. I think kithian is categorizing worlds as penumbra expect for Earth. I mean if Middle Kingdom or Middle World is Earth, and Lower World/Kingdom is the Videre Mortem(Penumbra of Low Umbra), I think Upper World/Kingdom is changes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It is about perspective. I don't think any of Nunnhei can see the Astral Videre since they are primordial and Videre Spiritus is suits for them. However, in Hsien case it could be different. They could categorize both Videre Spiritus(Penumbra of Middle Umbra) and Astral Videre as one, and name it as Upper World.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">However, one other think is that &quot;High Umbra&quot; could be &quot;banal&quot;, since it is about concepts rather than individual dreams. Sometimes I think it as Dreaming's young evil twin.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Dreaming is explicitly not the Umbra, though. That's why Spirit Link is an Art distinct from any that permit travel to the Deep Dreaming and other various otherworldly locales in Changeling. Also, Mage is not a particularly good guidebook to the rest of the WoD, again, given the issue of how its perspective of the Umbra disagrees severely with what you find in Werewolf, and other games are more likely to side with the game that doesn't declare outer space to be the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, in Werewolf, you can go to the Aetherial Realm, travel to another planet, and step sideways. It's a bad idea if you don't have Adaptation, though, since it lands you back in the physical realm, on another planet, which has very adverse environmental hazards to worry over. You could also do this just out in the vastness of space, but that would tend to be an even worse idea than being on most planets. The Aetherial Realm has an existence of spirit apart from the very physical reaches of space outside of Earth's atmosphere. This is in addition to being able to travel to what other people have described as something very like the Dreamspeakers' perspective on what the Deep Umbra is, and probably a number of other Traditions' as well. When it comes to videre theory, Werewolf just gives no shits.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T00:41:18-07:00","id":852273,"title":"","content":"there were occasional references to Heavenly realms for KOTE so I assumed that was their &quot;connection&quot; to the High Umbra as a counter point to the Yomi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T07:52:21-07:00","id":852434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/849744-where-actually-middle-world-and-upper-world-is?p=852273#post852273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there were occasional references to Heavenly realms for KOTE so I assumed that was their &amp;quot;connection&amp;quot; to the High Umbra as a counter point to the Yomi</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes! You're right. <br /> <br /> Asian mages would've interacted with the High Umbra too. Do they use the Western terminology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:02:53-07:00","id":852583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/849744-where-actually-middle-world-and-upper-world-is?p=852434#post852434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, yes! You're right.<br /> <br /> Asian mages would've interacted with the High Umbra too. Do they use the Western terminology?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only time the High Umbra was mentioned in Dragons of the East, it was using that term (on the last page of the book; there wasn't much there on it at all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}